1
00:00:02,430 --> 00:00:06,150
Leone, stop! We don't have time 
for something so unimportant!

2
00:00:06,150 --> 00:00:10,860
Unimportant? There's nothing 
more important to me right now!

3
00:00:13,540 --> 00:00:15,520
I see. You've grown.

4
00:00:15,840 --> 00:00:16,980
I won't let you get away!

5
00:00:20,160 --> 00:00:21,240
Leone!

6
00:00:22,810 --> 00:00:24,080
Don't move.

7
00:00:24,080 --> 00:00:26,550
I'd prefer you stay out of this.

8
00:00:26,550 --> 00:00:31,010
We don't want to hurt the 
daughter of the Arcia family.

9
00:00:31,010 --> 00:00:33,790
My father may be the Chancellor,

10
00:00:33,790 --> 00:00:37,970
but I'm only an academy student, 
and yet they know who I am...

11
00:00:38,510 --> 00:00:41,980
Just who are the Bloodchain Brigade?

12
00:00:57,110 --> 00:01:00,070
<u>Reborn</u>

13
00:00:57,110 --> 00:01:00,070
to Master the Blade
     From Hero-King to Extraordinary Squire

14
00:00:57,110 --> 00:01:00,070
to Master the Blade
From Hero-King to Extraordinary Squire

15
00:02:13,060 --> 00:02:16,900
Episode 10    The Plan to Attack a Highlander

16
00:02:16,910 --> 00:02:19,990
Mother and Father are gone!

17
00:02:19,990 --> 00:02:23,770
But for the people of Almen 
who were left behind...

18
00:02:23,770 --> 00:02:27,780
I can never forgive you!

19
00:02:27,780 --> 00:02:33,240
And if you lose Almen, 
you'll have nothing else left!

20
00:02:35,460 --> 00:02:39,770
The royal court has decided to offer up 
Almen to the Hierarch Highlanders

21
00:02:39,770 --> 00:02:44,180
to restore relations with them.

22
00:02:44,180 --> 00:02:46,640
But why would they do that?

23
00:02:46,640 --> 00:02:50,810
It's outlived its purpose as a place from 
which to monitor the frozen Prismer.

24
00:02:51,630 --> 00:02:54,660
I suppose they feel they have 
nothing to lose by offering it up.

25
00:02:54,660 --> 00:02:56,590
That's not right, though!

26
00:02:56,590 --> 00:02:59,250
Where's the justice in that?

27
00:03:00,230 --> 00:03:04,650
If you must rage against someone, 
direct your ire toward your foolish king

28
00:03:04,650 --> 00:03:08,210
who'd hand over his own people 
to curry favor with Highlanders.

29
00:03:08,210 --> 00:03:11,280
The Hyral Menas will be 
handed over in four days.

30
00:03:11,280 --> 00:03:13,980
The Highlander emissary will come by boat.

31
00:03:15,130 --> 00:03:18,240
We'll attack and kill the 
emissary when they arrive.

32
00:03:18,240 --> 00:03:22,090
Our only enemies are the Highlanders, who 
are trying to steal the very land from us.

33
00:03:22,090 --> 00:03:24,890
You're telling us your plan?

34
00:03:25,470 --> 00:03:28,060
What are you plotting?

35
00:03:28,060 --> 00:03:30,740
If you'd like to try something of your own,

36
00:03:30,740 --> 00:03:34,020
feel free to take advantage 
of the chaos we'll cause.

37
00:03:34,020 --> 00:03:37,230
But don't get in our way.

38
00:03:37,230 --> 00:03:39,490
And you think we'll just believe you?

39
00:03:39,810 --> 00:03:42,220
That's up to you.

40
00:03:42,220 --> 00:03:43,960
Now, goodbye.

41
00:03:43,960 --> 00:03:44,860
Brother!

42
00:03:47,680 --> 00:03:51,080
But I... No matter what your reason is...

43
00:03:51,080 --> 00:03:53,870
Do what you think is best.

44
00:03:53,870 --> 00:03:56,110
Nobody will stop you.

45
00:03:57,060 --> 00:03:59,200
But... You've grown.

46
00:03:59,630 --> 00:04:01,810
I can't do a thing for you,

47
00:04:02,300 --> 00:04:03,550
but that makes me happy.

48
00:04:04,180 --> 00:04:05,730
Keep it up.

49
00:04:11,220 --> 00:04:12,250
Leone...

50
00:04:12,930 --> 00:04:15,770
We need to head back and tell everyone.

51
00:04:17,700 --> 00:04:23,730
So you're saying that if we don't stop them, 
the Highland will take Ripple?

52
00:04:23,730 --> 00:04:26,580
And the town of Almen, to boot!

53
00:04:26,580 --> 00:04:29,160
That's just not right!

54
00:04:29,480 --> 00:04:32,110
Yes. We have to do something.

55
00:04:32,110 --> 00:04:34,220
But what?

56
00:04:34,750 --> 00:04:36,970
I have a plan.

57
00:04:38,190 --> 00:04:40,530
I see.

58
00:04:40,530 --> 00:04:42,490
That would work!

59
00:04:42,490 --> 00:04:44,270
But it's too reckless!

60
00:04:44,270 --> 00:04:48,770
Every time Chris says something, 
it's either reckless or insane.

61
00:04:48,770 --> 00:04:50,240
Yeah...

62
00:04:50,240 --> 00:04:51,780
Agreed.

63
00:04:53,980 --> 00:04:57,190
In a sense, they trust you, Inglis.

64
00:04:58,390 --> 00:05:01,750
We'll go with Inglis's idea, then.

65
00:05:01,750 --> 00:05:04,370
I'll get things started on my end first!

66
00:05:04,360 --> 00:05:06,820
Four Days Later

67
00:05:09,640 --> 00:05:11,540
Wh-What is this?

68
00:05:11,540 --> 00:05:15,450
What do you mean? 
They're maid outfits, of course.

69
00:05:15,450 --> 00:05:21,260
They're going to infiltrate the court 
under the guise of part-time servants.

70
00:05:21,260 --> 00:05:22,840
These maid outfits are great, huh?

71
00:05:22,840 --> 00:05:23,650
Yup!

72
00:05:24,200 --> 00:05:28,520
Principal Miliera, 
was there really no better way?

73
00:05:28,520 --> 00:05:32,300
I thought it was a great idea!

74
00:05:32,300 --> 00:05:35,840
One that takes full advantage 
of their cuteness!

75
00:05:36,190 --> 00:05:38,790
It'll be okay, Silva!

76
00:05:38,790 --> 00:05:42,740
When the Bloodchain Brigade 
comes to attack, we'll defeat them!

77
00:05:43,150 --> 00:05:46,730
While protecting the king 
and the Highlander emissary.

78
00:05:46,730 --> 00:05:48,220
Don't forget that.

79
00:05:48,600 --> 00:05:50,090
Okay!

80
00:05:50,090 --> 00:05:51,570
Good grief...

81
00:05:52,530 --> 00:05:55,540
When are they handing over Ripple?

82
00:05:55,850 --> 00:05:59,850
Right after the ceremony at the court.

83
00:05:59,850 --> 00:06:04,470
We wanted a little more time, 
but the royal guards weren't having it.

84
00:06:04,470 --> 00:06:09,120
But at the start they were saying, 
"Hand her over immediately!"

85
00:06:09,120 --> 00:06:10,830
This is a major victory!

86
00:06:10,830 --> 00:06:13,510
All thanks to Silva.

87
00:06:13,510 --> 00:06:15,780
I have a brother in the Royal Guard.

88
00:06:15,780 --> 00:06:19,470
I wasn't sure about going to him for help, 
but it didn't feel like we had a choice.

89
00:06:19,870 --> 00:06:23,870
While the royal guards are 
busy protecting the court,

90
00:06:23,870 --> 00:06:27,370
Silva and I will feed Ripple our mana, 
making her summon magicite beasts

91
00:06:27,370 --> 00:06:29,720
until there aren't any more left to summon.

92
00:06:29,720 --> 00:06:35,330
Then there'll be no reason 
to take her back to the Highland.

93
00:06:35,330 --> 00:06:37,340
It's a little crazy, but it'll work!

94
00:06:37,340 --> 00:06:39,310
It's not a little crazy. It's insane.

95
00:06:39,960 --> 00:06:42,140
But we don't have a choice.

96
00:06:42,850 --> 00:06:45,790
I'll be counting on you two. 
For Ripple's sake, too.

97
00:06:47,650 --> 00:06:49,450
Wh-What?

98
00:06:49,450 --> 00:06:53,590
Silva, do you like Ripple?

99
00:06:54,650 --> 00:06:56,230
Don't be ridiculous!

100
00:06:56,720 --> 00:06:58,380
Oh, my...

101
00:06:58,380 --> 00:07:01,020
You don't have to hide it!

102
00:07:01,020 --> 00:07:05,100
I do not! It would be most improper 
to think of a Hyral Menas that way.

103
00:07:05,690 --> 00:07:08,490
I do respect her deeply...

104
00:07:08,490 --> 00:07:10,910
Respect?

105
00:07:10,910 --> 00:07:13,660
When I was young, she saved my life.

106
00:07:14,370 --> 00:07:18,280
There was a sudden rain 
of Prism Flow one day.

107
00:07:18,280 --> 00:07:20,580
A friend and I were attacked 
by a magicite beast.

108
00:07:21,460 --> 00:07:25,580
We both ran... and he died protecting me.

109
00:07:26,300 --> 00:07:30,750
I was weak, and so he, 
a Runeless, had to die.

110
00:07:32,030 --> 00:07:36,430
Just as I thought it was all over, 
Ripple saved me.

111
00:07:42,360 --> 00:07:45,120
She held me as I cried, and she said...

112
00:07:45,740 --> 00:07:47,250
Get stronger.

113
00:07:47,250 --> 00:07:49,850
For the sake of your friend 
who protected you.

114
00:07:49,850 --> 00:07:54,720
And so you can protect dozens—
no, hundreds of times as many people more.

115
00:07:56,190 --> 00:07:59,190
Those words are what made me who I am today.

116
00:07:59,590 --> 00:08:05,010
I trained hard every day, so that I 
could be someone who protects others.

117
00:08:05,490 --> 00:08:08,580
<i>So he didn't hate the Runeless after all.</i>

118
00:08:08,580 --> 00:08:13,560
<i>He wanted to keep them from danger, and he 
was willing to sacrifice his own life for it.</i>

119
00:08:14,390 --> 00:08:19,120
I'm sorry for making you 
remember something like that.

120
00:08:19,120 --> 00:08:21,790
It was a long time ago. 
Don't worry about it.

121
00:08:21,790 --> 00:08:25,430
Is the reason you use a gun Artifact...

122
00:08:25,820 --> 00:08:30,920
Yes. I thought it would make it 
easier to fight alongside Ripple.

123
00:08:31,510 --> 00:08:33,370
That's wonderful...

124
00:08:33,370 --> 00:08:35,870
I'm sure Ripple will be very happy.

125
00:08:36,160 --> 00:08:40,530
Ripple remembered Silva.

126
00:08:41,090 --> 00:08:45,320
She looked upset... I don't know why.

127
00:08:45,930 --> 00:08:50,290
No, it's probably because I'm not 
strong enough for her to rely on me.

128
00:08:50,290 --> 00:08:51,610
That's not...

129
00:08:51,610 --> 00:08:54,430
Either way, we need to carry out the plan.

130
00:08:55,050 --> 00:08:57,890
I don't want Ripple to be taken 
from our country yet.

131
00:08:58,270 --> 00:09:01,800
Yes. And that's why we need 
to do our best tomorrow!

132
00:09:01,800 --> 00:09:04,980
Leave it to us, Silva!

133
00:09:04,980 --> 00:09:07,500
Right. I'll do my best on my end, too.

134
00:09:07,930 --> 00:09:13,940
No, I'd like to meet up with you guys 
and join the fight, so take your time.

135
00:09:15,950 --> 00:09:18,350
Just how obsessed
are you with fighting?

136
00:09:22,080 --> 00:09:25,660
New girls! Come help over here!

137
00:09:25,980 --> 00:09:27,180
Okay!

138
00:09:27,960 --> 00:09:29,710
It looks great!

139
00:09:29,710 --> 00:09:32,090
The food at the court's 
really something else.

140
00:09:32,410 --> 00:09:35,350
Rani, you ate too much. 
There's no shrimp left.

141
00:09:35,350 --> 00:09:38,530
And just how much meat 
are <i>you</i> going to eat, Chris?

142
00:09:40,090 --> 00:09:43,370
I'm eating a little from everything 
so they don't find out!

143
00:09:44,260 --> 00:09:46,600
It's a waste, too!

144
00:09:46,600 --> 00:09:50,710
When the Bloodchain Brigade comes, 
nobody's going to get to eat this food.

145
00:09:55,690 --> 00:09:58,240
Nobody can know about the attack.

146
00:09:58,240 --> 00:10:02,260
We don't want to talk about it and have 
them think we're co-conspirators.

147
00:10:02,650 --> 00:10:05,290
You say that, but you're 
just trying to make sure

148
00:10:05,290 --> 00:10:08,510
you've got as many enemies 
to fight as possible, right?

149
00:10:08,510 --> 00:10:09,990
That's right.

150
00:10:09,990 --> 00:10:11,340
Chris...

151
00:10:12,120 --> 00:10:16,240
Well, whatever. Until that 
time comes, we have to work!

152
00:10:17,630 --> 00:10:20,980
Oh, the king has arrived!

153
00:10:21,300 --> 00:10:22,900
King Carius!

154
00:10:22,900 --> 00:10:25,120
Hail to the king!

155
00:10:25,120 --> 00:10:29,470
Your Majesty! Your Majesty, King Carius!

156
00:10:29,470 --> 00:10:32,930
The king's got a Special-class rune, huh?

157
00:10:33,310 --> 00:10:36,380
He must be strong. 
It'll be easy to protect him.

158
00:10:36,380 --> 00:10:38,050
We don't know that for sure.

159
00:10:39,150 --> 00:10:43,910
<i>If you're doing your job as king, 
you won't have any time left to practice.</i>

160
00:10:44,240 --> 00:10:45,750
<i>I know that firsthand.</i>

161
00:10:46,980 --> 00:10:51,340
Today, I'm pleased to welcome 
an emissary from the Highland.

162
00:10:51,840 --> 00:10:55,620
They've promised to send a new Hyral Menas,

163
00:10:55,620 --> 00:10:59,040
who will lead our kingdom 
to even greater glory.

164
00:10:59,040 --> 00:11:01,830
What about Almen?

165
00:11:01,830 --> 00:11:04,740
Maybe they don't have to 
hand it over anymore.

166
00:11:04,740 --> 00:11:10,170
That's not it. At times like these, 
you just say the good things, not the bad.

167
00:11:10,170 --> 00:11:12,030
That's kind of sneaky!

168
00:11:12,590 --> 00:11:15,120
Now, let us welcome the emissary.

169
00:11:16,240 --> 00:11:18,850
Everyone, be on your best behavior.

170
00:11:18,850 --> 00:11:19,540
Yes, sire.

171
00:11:21,400 --> 00:11:23,990
Highlander Arch Lord
(Great General) Ivel

172
00:11:23,990 --> 00:11:26,720
Wow, he's cute!

173
00:11:26,720 --> 00:11:29,020
His eyes and hair are such pretty colors.

174
00:11:29,020 --> 00:11:30,070
Yeah.

175
00:11:30,290 --> 00:11:34,800
Allow me to introduce you all. 
This is the Highlander emissary, Lord Ivel.

176
00:11:35,080 --> 00:11:38,710
Despite his young age, 
he is already a great general.

177
00:11:38,710 --> 00:11:40,730
Oh, is that true?

178
00:11:40,730 --> 00:11:44,510
Then he must be of a higher rank 
than a typical emissary.

179
00:11:44,510 --> 00:11:49,880
Emissaries who get sent to the surface 
are just low-level foreign officers.

180
00:11:49,880 --> 00:11:54,220
I bear the rank of Arch Lord 
and command the Chief Hierarch's armies.

181
00:11:52,340 --> 00:11:55,250
I take it all back. He's not cute at all!

182
00:11:54,220 --> 00:11:56,320
I'm nothing like them.

183
00:11:55,250 --> 00:11:56,310
True.

184
00:11:56,310 --> 00:11:57,760
Wonderful!

185
00:11:57,760 --> 00:11:59,640
It's an honor to see him!

186
00:11:59,640 --> 00:12:02,290
This is a day I'll remember forever!

187
00:12:00,550 --> 00:12:02,440
I don't like this.

188
00:12:02,440 --> 00:12:05,730
Everybody sucking up 
to that mean little kid.

189
00:12:05,730 --> 00:12:07,170
Yeah.

190
00:12:07,170 --> 00:12:10,340
Hey, Chris! Pay attention!

191
00:12:14,550 --> 00:12:16,470
This is hilarious!

192
00:12:16,470 --> 00:12:22,020
We get a whole city just for swapping out 
one defective Hyral Menas!

193
00:12:22,250 --> 00:12:25,750
You're losing the lives of your fellow men, 
you're losing a valuable asset,

194
00:12:25,750 --> 00:12:28,760
and you're still trying to suck up to me!

195
00:12:28,760 --> 00:12:29,960
You're all crazy.

196
00:12:30,950 --> 00:12:35,460
You fools don't realize that 
any one of you could be next.

197
00:12:31,170 --> 00:12:34,560
I hate to say it, but he's right.

198
00:12:34,560 --> 00:12:35,810
Yup.

199
00:12:35,810 --> 00:12:41,050
Well, for my part, 
it's easier to deal with fools.

200
00:12:41,050 --> 00:12:43,910
Thanks. For being so stupid.

201
00:12:46,730 --> 00:12:49,500
There's no need to thank us, Lord Ivel.

202
00:12:49,500 --> 00:12:52,950
We are fools, as you say.

203
00:12:52,950 --> 00:12:55,730
And I, as king, am the 
greatest fool of them all.

204
00:12:55,730 --> 00:13:01,340
I only hope that you will teach us 
to be as smart as you.

205
00:13:02,270 --> 00:13:03,990
Please teach us...

206
00:13:05,310 --> 00:13:08,820
I don't want to see this. It's pathetic.

207
00:13:08,820 --> 00:13:11,760
Yeah? It's kinda interesting, though.

208
00:13:12,330 --> 00:13:15,260
<i>Normally, one would respond 
to such provocations with anger.</i>

209
00:13:15,260 --> 00:13:16,700
<i>For him to react this way...</i>

210
00:13:16,700 --> 00:13:21,350
<i>Either he's not human, or he has 
something he truly believes in.</i>

211
00:13:21,700 --> 00:13:25,410
You're interesting, for a fool.

212
00:13:27,380 --> 00:13:29,030
Magicite beasts!

213
00:13:30,240 --> 00:13:31,520
They're here!

214
00:13:31,790 --> 00:13:33,430
Let's do it, Chris!

215
00:13:33,430 --> 00:13:35,220
Huh?

216
00:13:48,840 --> 00:13:50,590
Who is that girl?

217
00:13:50,590 --> 00:13:54,300
I'm a maid, so it's my job 
to clean up the banquet hall!

218
00:13:54,720 --> 00:13:56,180
Rani, you take—

219
00:13:58,890 --> 00:14:00,260
What was that?

220
00:14:01,200 --> 00:14:03,930
<i>I've never seen that attack before.</i>

221
00:14:03,930 --> 00:14:07,120
Seal the exits! Prepare for 
an attack from the windows!

222
00:14:07,390 --> 00:14:10,570
Protect the king and the emissary!

223
00:14:10,570 --> 00:14:11,440
Yes, sir!

224
00:14:14,940 --> 00:14:16,630
How obnoxious.

225
00:14:18,340 --> 00:14:21,110
Die!

226
00:14:24,830 --> 00:14:26,140
I can't move...

227
00:14:26,140 --> 00:14:27,860
L-Let me go!

228
00:14:27,860 --> 00:14:28,840
No.

229
00:14:28,840 --> 00:14:32,810
The Highlanders must be stopped 
before they take all our homes!

230
00:14:31,850 --> 00:14:34,510
Is he with the Bloodchain Brigade?

231
00:14:34,510 --> 00:14:37,350
Hey. Nobody asked for your help.

232
00:14:37,350 --> 00:14:40,700
Did you think a weakling like him 
could so much as scratch me?

233
00:14:40,700 --> 00:14:42,600
My apologies.

234
00:14:43,000 --> 00:14:44,540
Well, it's fine.

235
00:14:44,540 --> 00:14:46,580
Restrain him.

236
00:14:47,390 --> 00:14:49,320
<i>The same light as before...</i>

237
00:15:07,350 --> 00:15:08,920
Chris, are you okay?!

238
00:15:09,190 --> 00:15:10,990
Y-Yeah.

239
00:15:10,990 --> 00:15:13,060
Not much scares you, huh?

240
00:15:13,060 --> 00:15:14,300
Thanks.

241
00:15:14,300 --> 00:15:17,530
Did you do that deliberately? 
That's disgusting!

242
00:15:17,530 --> 00:15:22,030
Yeah? If anything's disgusting, 
it's inviting someone to a banquet

243
00:15:22,030 --> 00:15:24,720
and then trying to kill them.

244
00:15:25,060 --> 00:15:29,900
N-No! I assure you, 
our country was not behind this!

245
00:15:29,900 --> 00:15:31,330
It was the Bloodchain Brigade,

246
00:15:31,330 --> 00:15:34,380
a group of rebels that have been 
active in our lands lately...

247
00:15:35,480 --> 00:15:39,310
I'm willing to believe that, 
but that's still a problem.

248
00:15:39,310 --> 00:15:40,700
A problem?

249
00:15:40,700 --> 00:15:46,170
Your incompetence put a 
Highlander emissary in danger.

250
00:15:46,650 --> 00:15:49,870
How do you intend to atone for that sin?

251
00:15:50,860 --> 00:15:53,460
Please, show mercy!

252
00:15:53,740 --> 00:15:57,810
I, Carius, am prepared 
to accept any punishment!

253
00:15:57,810 --> 00:15:59,850
Your Majesty!

254
00:15:59,850 --> 00:16:02,260
No, that's not good enough.

255
00:16:02,890 --> 00:16:07,970
An apology only means something 
when it's between two equals.

256
00:16:08,400 --> 00:16:10,950
But the Highland and 
the surface aren't equal.

257
00:16:11,550 --> 00:16:14,790
You're just the boss of 
a group of cattle we keep.

258
00:16:14,790 --> 00:16:17,780
And an apology from cattle 
means nothing.

259
00:16:18,460 --> 00:16:19,650
So...

260
00:16:26,970 --> 00:16:30,210
I'm taking an arm.

261
00:16:30,210 --> 00:16:32,220
Y-Your Majesty!

262
00:16:32,220 --> 00:16:33,440
Damn you!

263
00:16:33,440 --> 00:16:35,550
Even if you're the Highland emissary...

264
00:16:35,830 --> 00:16:38,290
Calm yourselves, everyone!

265
00:16:38,290 --> 00:16:43,250
Anyone who harms the emissary will 
be executed in the name of the king!

266
00:16:43,250 --> 00:16:45,340
Y-Yes, sire...

267
00:16:45,950 --> 00:16:50,700
Thank you for your mercy, Lord Ivel.

268
00:16:50,930 --> 00:16:51,780
Your Majesty...

269
00:16:51,780 --> 00:16:55,490
Chris, is this really okay?

270
00:16:55,490 --> 00:16:57,190
Is this really right?

271
00:16:57,190 --> 00:16:58,380
It's not...

272
00:16:58,380 --> 00:17:00,030
That's up to the individual, isn't it?

273
00:17:00,340 --> 00:17:03,240
What you think is right, is right.

274
00:17:03,740 --> 00:17:05,810
<i>Everyone really does have their own ideas.</i>

275
00:17:05,810 --> 00:17:09,580
<i>Some pledge loyalty to the Highlanders, 
to keep their people alive.</i>

276
00:17:10,150 --> 00:17:14,160
<i>Others try to become stronger, 
to become equals to the Highlanders.</i>

277
00:17:14,480 --> 00:17:17,640
<i>What will come of the contrast between them?</i>

278
00:17:17,640 --> 00:17:21,380
<i>Well, that's for the people 
of this era to decide.</i>

279
00:17:21,950 --> 00:17:24,980
Anyway, Rani, we have something 
we have to hurry and do.

280
00:17:29,350 --> 00:17:30,640
Excuse me.

281
00:17:33,290 --> 00:17:35,280
We'll try to heal your wound.

282
00:17:35,280 --> 00:17:36,100
Rani.

283
00:17:37,240 --> 00:17:38,520
I'll give it a shot.

284
00:17:45,390 --> 00:17:46,700
It's healing!

285
00:17:47,310 --> 00:17:50,730
<i>This is more difficult 
than what she did for Silva...</i>

286
00:17:52,520 --> 00:17:55,250
<i>Rani works hard.</i>

287
00:17:55,630 --> 00:17:58,140
Hey, what are you doing?

288
00:17:58,140 --> 00:17:59,910
We are healing him.

289
00:17:59,910 --> 00:18:01,830
May we continue?

290
00:18:01,830 --> 00:18:03,860
I don't mind.

291
00:18:03,860 --> 00:18:05,230
Thank you.

292
00:18:05,230 --> 00:18:11,070
But I'm going to take someone 
else's arm instead.

293
00:18:11,070 --> 00:18:17,020
Now, who's going to offer up 
their arm to make me happy?

294
00:18:18,140 --> 00:18:20,000
If my healing comes at 
such a cost, I cannot...

295
00:18:20,490 --> 00:18:23,940
Try and take my arm, then!

296
00:18:24,180 --> 00:18:28,160
<i>It'll give me a chance to see 
that power up close.</i>

297
00:18:28,160 --> 00:18:29,610
Sure.

298
00:18:29,610 --> 00:18:32,630
Normally, I wouldn't care 
about the arm of a Runeless,

299
00:18:33,120 --> 00:18:36,960
but I can't wait to see that smile 
on your face turn to a scream.

300
00:18:36,960 --> 00:18:38,990
C-Chris!

301
00:18:38,990 --> 00:18:40,840
It's fine, Rani.

302
00:18:40,840 --> 00:18:42,670
Just keep healing His Majesty.

303
00:18:42,670 --> 00:18:46,360
I look forward to hearing 
how you'll shriek in pain.

304
00:18:47,150 --> 00:18:50,500
Yeah, it's not just mana moving.

305
00:18:50,500 --> 00:18:52,850
It's a bunch of different 
wavelengths mixed together.

306
00:18:52,850 --> 00:18:54,680
You don't know anything!

307
00:18:54,680 --> 00:18:56,200
Now, here I go!

308
00:18:56,200 --> 00:18:59,130
I won't stop, no matter how much you cry!

309
00:19:01,490 --> 00:19:02,550
What?

310
00:19:03,570 --> 00:19:06,650
H-Hey, that was the same 
thing he did before, right?

311
00:19:04,480 --> 00:19:07,400
<i>I'd turned down its power 
so he couldn't sense it,</i>

312
00:19:06,650 --> 00:19:08,670
Y-Yeah, but...

313
00:19:07,400 --> 00:19:10,330
<i>but I definitely activated 
an Aether Shell just now!</i>

314
00:19:10,330 --> 00:19:12,770
<i>And his power exceeded even that...</i>

315
00:19:13,250 --> 00:19:16,350
<i>I like this maid outfit, 
so I'm sorry to see it damaged,</i>

316
00:19:16,350 --> 00:19:18,230
<i>but that was a most impressive display!</i>

317
00:19:18,620 --> 00:19:21,440
Amazing! That was amazing!

318
00:19:21,440 --> 00:19:23,810
D-Damn you!

319
00:19:28,820 --> 00:19:32,320
Maybe it's not that powerful after all?

320
00:19:32,320 --> 00:19:35,820
But it definitely killed the 
assassin and took the king's arm!

321
00:19:36,200 --> 00:19:39,140
I see! It's not just mana.

322
00:19:39,140 --> 00:19:43,020
It's similar, but using 
something more powerful!

323
00:19:43,670 --> 00:19:45,480
It's Mana Refinement!

324
00:19:45,480 --> 00:19:47,620
It increases the purity 
and efficiency of mana!

325
00:19:48,080 --> 00:19:51,250
You surface dwellers shouldn't 
be able to defend against it!

326
00:19:51,250 --> 00:19:52,560
But you...

327
00:19:52,560 --> 00:19:55,510
Quality over quantity, right?

328
00:19:55,510 --> 00:19:59,640
If it evolves along that path, 
it might catch up to aether someday!

329
00:19:59,640 --> 00:20:00,970
Wonderful!

330
00:20:01,530 --> 00:20:04,730
I can't understand your power at all...

331
00:20:04,730 --> 00:20:08,340
What is that power? Who are you?

332
00:20:08,760 --> 00:20:09,930
Who the hell are you?!

333
00:20:13,320 --> 00:20:15,120
Just a maid. Why?

334
00:20:15,560 --> 00:20:17,490
Damn you...

335
00:20:17,490 --> 00:20:19,400
Don't you <i>dare</i> mock me!

336
00:20:22,270 --> 00:20:24,740
Why? It's not working at all!

337
00:20:25,670 --> 00:20:27,370
Even if you're a child,

338
00:20:27,370 --> 00:20:31,040
I don't think it's a good idea to keep 
touching a girl's breasts like that.

339
00:20:31,530 --> 00:20:33,270
Oh, sorry.

340
00:20:34,980 --> 00:20:36,540
Now, continue!

341
00:20:36,540 --> 00:20:39,460
Please, cut off my arm!

342
00:20:39,460 --> 00:20:42,520
Inglis, was it?

343
00:20:42,520 --> 00:20:44,620
You're no maid!

344
00:20:44,620 --> 00:20:48,180
Tell me your true identity! 
What are you planning?!

345
00:20:48,180 --> 00:20:50,210
My true identity?

346
00:20:50,210 --> 00:20:51,600
Actually...

347
00:20:51,600 --> 00:20:56,010
I'm a part-time maid! I wanted money 
to buy lots of yummy food.

348
00:20:56,360 --> 00:20:59,610
So you're not going to answer me?

349
00:20:59,610 --> 00:21:00,600
Then...

350
00:21:00,600 --> 00:21:03,110
At least show me your power!

351
00:21:03,110 --> 00:21:05,610
Come on! Attack me!

352
00:21:05,610 --> 00:21:10,370
But weren't you the one who wanted 
my arm instead of the king's?

353
00:21:10,370 --> 00:21:12,030
Forget that!

354
00:21:12,030 --> 00:21:13,820
Come on! Attack me!

355
00:21:13,820 --> 00:21:18,940
Personally, I'd love nothing more 
than to duel you, but...

356
00:21:18,940 --> 00:21:19,920
Stand down.

357
00:21:20,620 --> 00:21:26,760
Even if it's what he wants, 
you must not harm a Highlander!

358
00:21:26,760 --> 00:21:29,230
You must...

359
00:21:30,060 --> 00:21:32,710
You really are a dumb animal.

360
00:21:32,710 --> 00:21:35,180
There's no point in trying to suck up to me.

361
00:21:36,150 --> 00:21:38,270
The reason that I, an Arch Lord,

362
00:21:38,270 --> 00:21:42,350
came all the way to the surface 
was not to bring you a Hyral Menas

363
00:21:42,350 --> 00:21:44,820
or repair relationships between our nations!

364
00:21:45,070 --> 00:21:47,280
The Chief Hierarch is angry!

365
00:21:47,280 --> 00:21:50,750
One day, this whole country 
will be wiped from the map.

366
00:21:51,200 --> 00:21:54,400
Then why did you come here?

367
00:21:54,400 --> 00:21:55,840
Because...

368
00:23:45,980 --> 00:23:50,980
m 0 0 l 100 0 100 100 0 100

369
00:23:45,980 --> 00:23:50,980
Please go 
home,
 Highlander!

370
00:23:45,980 --> 00:23:50,980
Comic by Kuromura Moto

